  "method": {
    "configs_per_recipe": "base (no delta), full_delta (Instruct weights == base + full delta on every tensor), factored_delta (base + factored delta per the recipe's rank map)",
    "streaming": "AirLLM-style layer streaming in our own NumPy runtime (concept from lyogavin/airllm, Apache 2.0; code ours): the eval never holds the model whole; per transformer block the weights are read from the sharded safetensors, the factored delta is added chunk-wise in place, all items pass through the block, and the block is released; the embedding is gathered row-wise; lm_head logits are computed only at answer positions",
    "factored_application": "rank map applies per layer type across all 28 blocks plus embed and lm_head (198 matrices); factors built with factored.quantize_delta's construction via one exact SVD per matrix sliced per rank (Gram-matrix exact SVD; validated against quantize_delta itself on block matrices, see build_validation; the two 151936-row matrices use the memory-bounded Gram variant with fp64 Gram accumulation, residuals recorded in build_validation)",
    "scoring": "chat-formatted prompt (ChatML format, system line 'You are Qwen, created by Alibaba Cloud. You are a helpful assistant.'); target logprob = summed log-probability of the answer tokens (Signet convention); accuracy = first-token accuracy; gap_closed = (factored - base) / (full - base) on mean target logprob",
    "forward_pass": "NumPy Qwen2.5 forward written for this pair (plain RoPE theta 1000000, RMSNorm eps 1e-6, GQA 28 Q / 4 KV heads, untied embeddings), streamed block by block; no external Signet battery exists for this pair, so it is validated by internal consistency (see forward_validation)",
    "stage1_role": "filter only: no winner is declared from Stage 1 matrix error; the ranking below is by Stage 2 task score",
    "repricing": "every recipe re-priced on real shapes with factored.storage_bytes before comparison; recipes were generated against the real-shape budget directly (see results/fifth_pair_check1.json), so generation totals and Stage 2 totals use the same basis",
